{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>If you take a pledge in pledge.</b> By means of a messenger of the court, as it is written: 'outside you shall stand,' etc. — but you shall not enter his house to take his pledge, and this is the meaning of 'you shall not be to him as a creditor.'" "<b>You shall restore it to him.</b> And if you ask: if so, the borrower will never repay his debt, since the lender restores his garment to him — one may answer that it deals only with a case where the court's messenger took it, not at the time of the loan, and gave it to the lender, and he is not commanded to return it to the borrower except for thirty days, for that is the court's timeframe, and after the time period he is permitted to sell it." "<b>You shall restore it to him.</b> This refers back to the pledge, which is masculine in form."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:52.179598191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}